---
import { Github, Coffee } from 'lucide-astro';
---
<section id="install" aria-labelledby="install-heading" class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-section sm:px-8">
  <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.2fr] lg:items-start" data-reveal-group>
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow mb-4 reveal">Install</p>
      <h2 id="install-heading" class="text-display font-light leading-[1.02] tracking-[-0.025em] reveal">
        Coming to Flathub.<br />Buildable today.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-md text-bone-dim reveal">
        Flathub will be the recommended path for most people. An AUR package is planned. Until then, build from source.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3 reveal">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" aria-disabled="true" href="https://flathub.org/">Flathub, soon</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://github.com/abullard1/quoth" rel="noopener"><Github size={16} stroke-width={1.75} /> GitHub</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://buymeacoffee.com/samuelbullard" rel="noopener"><Coffee size={16} stroke-width={1.75} /> Buy me a coffee</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="surface overflow-hidden rounded-2xl">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b hairline px-5 py-3">
          <span class="eyebrow">Build from source</span>
          <span class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-500">bash</span>
        </div>
        <pre class="overflow-x-auto p-5 font-mono text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-bone-dim"><code>git clone https://github.com/abullard1/quoth.git
cd quoth
uv sync                  <span class="text-ink-500"># Python dependencies</span>
bash lib/build_helper.sh <span class="text-ink-500"># whisper.cpp C shim</span>
uv run quoth</code></pre>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-400">
        Needs GTK4, libadwaita, PyGObject, GStreamer with the PipeWire plugin, gtk4-layer-shell, wl-clipboard, wtype, a Vulkan loader and whisper.cpp from your distro. OpenVINO is optional for the Intel NPU path, keyd for the global hotkey.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
